## 7. Resonance and aromaticity: topology in L2 (without mysticism)

### 7.1 Resonance (standard)
Multiple Lewis structures represent one quantum state.

**UAF mapping:** resonance is model uncertainty: several discrete symbolic decompositions map to the same underlying electron density attractor.

### 7.2 Aromaticity (Hückel rule)
For planar cyclic conjugated systems:

\[
4n+2 \;\pi\text{-electrons} \Rightarrow \text{aromatic (stabilized)}
\]

**UAF mapping:** aromaticity is a **stability invariant**: a closed predictive loop in electron phase space that yields unusually low energy (low \(\Delta G\)). It is one of the cleanest bridges from L0 topology to L2 chemical stability.

