## 10. The periodic table as L2’s “model atlas”

The periodic table is not a list. It is an atlas of valence subspaces.

- Groups correspond to similar valence structure (same low-energy bonding subspace dimension).
- Periods correspond to shell completion (quantized capacity changes).

**UAF mapping:** the periodic table is a compressed index of predictable bonding behavior.

This is the reason chemistry is learnable: the periodic table is a high-NPG compression of L0 microphysics.

